@startuml
title DineFlow - Pre-Order Creation and Checkout Exit
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

autonumber
actor Customer
participant "OrderService" as Order
note over Customer,Order
Start: customer owns a CONFIRMED reservation (P-PAY).
No payment attempt exists; the draft creates no extra table hold.
end note
Customer -> Order : createPreOrder(reservationId, readyAt)
Order --> Customer : DRAFT + order reference + proposed checkout deadline
loop Each selected dish
 Customer -> Order : addItem(orderId, itemId, quantity)
 Order --> Customer : item accepted / input or availability error
end
Customer -> Order : quote(orderId)
alt Invalid or empty order / invalid quote
 Order --> Customer : correct draft; no payment attempt
else Valid quote
 Order --> Customer : amount + currency + quote validity
 alt Customer confirms before deadline
  ref over Customer,Order
  Payment initiation and verified outcome
  See payment-sequence.puml
  end ref
 else Customer explicitly cancels before initiation
  Customer -> Order : cancelUnpaid(orderId)
  note over Order : PreOrder = CANCELLED; Payment absent.
  Order --> Customer : pre-order cancelled; reservation unchanged
 else Customer leaves without confirming
  note over Customer,Order : No confirmation message; this is not a rejected payment.
  opt Draft still unpaid at proposed finite deadline
   Order -> Order : expireUnpaid(orderId)
   note over Order : PreOrder = EXPIRED; Payment absent.
  end
 end
end
note over Customer,Order
End: DRAFT correction, payment subprocess, CANCELLED, or EXPIRED.
Reservation stays CONFIRMED until separate cancellation / booked end.
Cancellation and initiation check state as one logical decision:
if initiation already won, reconcile instead of claiming no charge exists.
Deadline trigger/duration remain D-04; no scheduler is selected.
end note
legend bottom
P-PAY proposed; FR-007-FR-008. Valid quote is an input to the separate payment scenario.
An abandoned draft is finite. It never creates an indefinite table hold.
endlegend
@enduml
